# Build context exclusions (change deploy-server-docker).
#
# The Dockerfile only needs core/ and server/. Everything else is either
# generated, per-user, or large, and shipping it to the Docker daemon makes
# every `docker compose build` slow: without this file the build context is
# tens of GB (server/target alone is ~24 GB) and the transfer dominates the
# build time even when the cargo steps are cached.

# Rust build output. Both the workspace-root target/ and the per-crate ones;
# server/target is the big one.
target/
**/target/

# Generated FFI / mobile build artifacts
uniffi/
ios/Frameworks/
android/app/src/main/jniLibs/
android/.gradle/
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/local.properties

# Node.js
node_modules/

# Version control and editor state
.git/
.gitignore
*.swp

# Runtime and per-deployment configuration
data/
backups/
.env
.env.*

# Local/CI compose and deployment docs are not needed inside the image
docker-compose.yml
docker-compose.prod.yml
.env.example

# Tests, docs, tooling
docs/
openspec/
scripts/
*.md
